{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"毒理学基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"dose-response","title":"剂量-反应关系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations/dose-response","wordCount":2078,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"adme","title":"吸收分布代谢排泄","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations/adme","wordCount":1876,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"toxicity-mechanisms","title":"毒性作用机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/environmental-science/environmental-toxicology/foundations/toxicity-mechanisms","wordCount":1852,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"毒理学基础\">毒理学基础</h1><p>这一章建立整个 hub 共用的概念工具箱。环境毒理学后面要讨论的每一种污染物、每一次暴露、每一份风险评估报告，最终都要回到这一章定义的三组基本问题上：效应随剂量如何变化、毒物在体内经历了什么、到达靶点后又做了什么。</p>\n<p>第一篇「剂量-反应关系」是基石中的基石。它把「某物质是否有毒」这个模糊判断，替换成「在多大剂量下、对谁、产生多强效应」这个可测量、可建模的连续问题。从 S 形曲线、<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mn>50</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{LD}_{50}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">LD</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">50</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> 与 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mn>50</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{EC}_{50}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">EC</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">50</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>，到 NOAEL、基准剂量（BMD），再到有阈与无阈之争——后面所有章节里出现的毒性基准点，都是在这条曲线上读出来的。</p>\n<p>第二篇「吸收分布代谢排泄」补上从外暴露到内剂量的转换。同样的环境浓度，为什么有的物质一晃而过、有的却在体内累积多年？答案藏在 ADME 四过程里。这一篇解释了亲脂性、代谢激活、半衰期等概念，它们既是生物富集的动力学根源，也是跨物种外推不确定性的来源。</p>\n<p>第三篇「毒性作用机制」回答最核心的「为什么」。氧化应激、共价结合、受体介导、酶抑制——不同污染物造成截然不同后果的分子根源都在这里，并由不良结局通路（AOP）框架串成可用于监管的因果链。</p>\n<p>读懂这三篇，就掌握了贯穿全 hub 的统一语言。建议先通读本章，再进入后续的污染物、归趋与风险章节。</p>\n"}